{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs",
  "item": "mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Source-tool tests publish OutlineId addresses and retain mapped NodeIds\n directly in dependencies. This required Domain method is unused in\n those flows; stable-path and filesystem-storage tests use other domains."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]` is valid.\n\n**Form.** It is a fenced commentary citation on an explicit function with a body. That is a permitted form, and it excuses only this function's zero execution. The commentary gives a substantive reason, not just difficulty.\n\n**The explanation matches the current source.**\n- The tests in `project_sources.rs#mod[tests]` use `Project` through `ProjectSources` source tools, `InspectionContext::read_source` and `Validator::refresh_evidence`. They publish `OutlineId` addresses (path and selector), and `Project/SourceNodes::source_node` maps them to the `\"source-node\"` `NodeId`.\n- Dependencies are `Dependency::Node(\"source-node\", fingerprint)`, and the tests assert them directly. None of that goes through `node_path`.\n- `node_path` has only a few callers: `graph.rs#fn[edge_fingerprint]`, `agent/tools.rs` `ToolAgent::run`, and `GraphSession::node` and `GraphSession::dispatch`.\n  - `edge_fingerprint` is reached only for outgoing-edge dependencies. `Project::outgoing_edges` always returns an empty list, so it never calls `node_path`.\n  - The `ToolAgent` and `GraphSession` code is not used by these tests. The validator test sets an agent config but only runs deterministic source reads.\n- `Project`'s `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` ignore the node and keep one record, so they don't use the path either.\n- The claim about other domains also holds. `tests/contracts.rs` (`Application`, `Relationships`) and `tests/storage.rs` (`StoredGraph`) exercise `node_path` for stable paths and filesystem-record keys.\n\nThe commentary agrees with the code and the surrounding tests, and I found no gap.",
